{"paper": "SSC-DelhiPoliceHC-10-Oct-2022-Shift3.pdf", "status": "ok", "mode": "sequential", "splitter": "qdot", "section_slice": true, "extracted_count": 20, "tagged_count": 20, "questions": [{"n": 1, "text": "In a workshop, Saral and Kanika are working on alternate days. Saral on the 1st day, Kanika on the 2nd day, Saral on the 3rd day and so on. Saral alone can complete the work in 15 days, while Kanika alone takes 18 days to finish the same work. In how many days will they complete the work if they work on alternate basis?", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Work", "sub": "alternate-days", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 2, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "0", "added": false}, {"text": "343", "added": false}, {"text": "2863", "added": false}, {"text": "392", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Algebra", "sub": "identities", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 3, "text": "The curved surface area of a right circular cylinder of height 14 cm is 88 cm2.The diameter of the base of cylinder is ________.", "options": [{"text": "4 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "2 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "1 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "3 cm", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 3D", "sub": "cylinder", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 4, "text": "The diameter of a circle is 35 cm. Find the length of the arc of a sector, if the area of the sector is 385 cm2", "options": [{"text": "44 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "42 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "48 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "40 cm", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 2D", "sub": "circle-sector-ring", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 5, "text": "Two printers were sold for Rs.12,000 each, one at a gain of 20% and the other at a loss of 20%. Find the loss or gain in the entire transaction.", "options": [{"text": "2.4% profit", "added": false}, {"text": "4% loss", "added": false}, {"text": "4% profit", "added": false}, {"text": "2.4% loss", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Profit-Loss", "sub": "successive-transactions", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 6, "text": "Salim borrowed ₹7,200 from the bank for some project at simple interest. After a period of 3 years, the amount will be ₹9,576. What was the rate of interest?", "options": [{"text": "10%", "added": false}, {"text": "9%", "added": false}, {"text": "12%", "added": false}, {"text": "11%", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Simple Interest", "sub": "rate-time-principal", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 7, "text": "The population of a city in 2014 was 8000000. If in 2015, there is an increment of 8%, in 2016, there is a decrement of 35% and in 2017, there is an increment of 65%, then what is the population of the city at the end of the year 2017?", "options": [{"text": "9635535", "added": false}, {"text": "8400278", "added": false}, {"text": "9266400", "added": false}, {"text": "7000000", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "successive-change", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 8, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "Neha, Keval, Ankit", "added": false}, {"text": "Ankit, Keval, Neha", "added": false}, {"text": "Ankit , Neha, Keval", "added": false}, {"text": "Neha, Ankit, Keval", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Data Interpretation", "sub": "table", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 9, "text": "A trader allows a discount of 12.5% for cash payment. How much percentage above the cost price must he mark his goods to make a profit of 20%?", "options": [{"text": "31.743%", "added": false}, {"text": "37.143%", "added": false}, {"text": "34.173%", "added": false}, {"text": "33.417%", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Discount", "sub": "mp-sp-relation", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 10, "text": "The HCF of two numbers is 6. Which of the following can NEVER be their LCM?", "options": [{"text": "24", "added": false}, {"text": "48", "added": false}, {"text": "60", "added": false}, {"text": "56", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "HCF-LCM", "sub": "hcf-lcm-of-numbers", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 11, "text": "The effective annual rate of interest corresponding to a nominal rate of 10% per annum payable half yearly is:", "options": [{"text": "5.50%", "added": false}, {"text": "10.25%", "added": false}, {"text": "10%", "added": false}, {"text": "5%", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Compound Interest", "sub": "compounding-frequency", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 12, "text": "A and B alone can complete a piece of work in 4 days and 8 days, respectively. In how many days will the work be completed, if they both work on alternate days starting with A?", "options": [{"text": "5 days", "added": false}, {"text": "6 days", "added": false}, {"text": "7 days", "added": false}, {"text": "4 days", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Work", "sub": "alternate-days", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 13, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "57", "added": false}, {"text": "62", "added": false}, {"text": "42", "added": false}, {"text": "72", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Algebra", "sub": "identities", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 14, "text": "Which of the following pair of numbers are Prime?", "options": [{"text": "47 and 27", "added": false}, {"text": "57 and 67", "added": false}, {"text": "77 and 97", "added": false}, {"text": "37 and 67", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Number System", "sub": "types-of-numbers", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 15, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Trigonometry", "sub": "identities", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 16, "text": "A metro train runs at the speed of 40 km/h from station A to station B covering a distance of 30 km. It stops at 5 stations in between, for 5 minutes at each station. What is the average speed (in km/h) of the trainfrom A to B?", "options": [{"text": "24.7", "added": false}, {"text": "25.7", "added": false}, {"text": "27.5", "added": false}, {"text": "22.5", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Speed-Distance", "sub": "average-speed", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 17, "text": "A policeman starts chasing a thief when he was 800 m ahead. The policeman and the thief run at the rate of 12 km/h and 9 km/h, respectively. What will be the distance between them after 10 minutes?", "options": [{"text": "300 m", "added": false}, {"text": "200 m", "added": false}, {"text": "100 m", "added": false}, {"text": "400 m", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Speed-Distance", "sub": "relative-speed", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 18, "text": "If (x - 1) is a factor of (x2 + 6kx - 7),then what is the value of k?", "options": [{"text": "4", "added": false}, {"text": "3", "added": false}, {"text": "1", "added": false}, {"text": "2", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Algebra", "sub": "polynomials-and-factorisation", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 19, "text": "The fourth proportional to 4x + 3, 7x + 2 and 9x +2, if x = 4 is:", "options": [{"text": "45", "added": false}, {"text": "58", "added": false}, {"text": "68", "added": false}, {"text": "60", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Ratio-Proportion", "sub": "proportion", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 20, "text": "If a cube has the same volume as surface area, then the length of the side is:", "options": [{"text": "2", "added": false}, {"text": "4", "added": false}, {"text": "8", "added": false}, {"text": "6", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_onl